    "updated_at": "2021-01-06T15:23:29Z",
    "body": "Hi @dmitry-mightydevops, This is a known issue we don't enable showing the version of terraform by default since getting the version of terraform can be very slow and if I remember correctly it will sometimes perform a network request to see if there is a new version available. \r\n\r\n```\r\n# Just terraform\r\n❯ hyperfine \"terraform version -json\"\r\nBenchmark #1: terraform version -json\r\n  Time (mean ± σ):      41.0 ms ±   8.8 ms    [User: 39.2 ms, System: 18.6 ms]\r\n  Range (min … max):    31.8 ms …  75.7 ms    57 runs\r\n \r\n# Single provider\r\n❯ hyperfine \"terraform version -json\"\r\nBenchmark #1: terraform version -json\r\n  Time (mean ± σ):     111.0 ms ±   9.9 ms    [User: 107.8 ms, System: 25.9 ms]\r\n  Range (min … max):   100.4 ms … 139.5 ms    21 runs\r\n ```\r\n\r\n@matchai I wonder if we should make this more obvious in the docs maybe with a warning box, what do you think?",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
